From f4c005e17b3622c85574075ccf082a3010835b8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:21:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 521/528] [DS4.1] Engram's token map, geometry and caps in
 vLLM; resident tables gather with TileLang

engram.py imported B12X at module level (b12x.preparation and
b12x.sequence.engram), so the model could not even be imported without it.
Serving reached B12X for the compressed-token map, the hash geometry and
the per-layer caps; a resident (device or RAM) table also used B12X's
lookup, prepared through B12X's preparation pass.

- common/engram_geometry.py: build_compressed_token_map, Geometry,
  build_geometry, is_prime_64 and EngramCaps, B12X's code (geometry.py,
  _impl.Caps, ple_hash.reference.is_prime_64 at 236ddff04a5f) with the same
  tables, primes, offsets, multipliers and checks.
- tilelang/engram_rows.py: engram_table_gather (vllm::dsv41_engram_table_
  gather), a resident shard's gather with B12X's lookup arithmetic (the
  value times its E8M0 scale, 2^-127 for byte 0 and NaN for 255, rounded
  to BF16) and its zeros: past the live count, for every token when the
  count is outside [0, tokens], and for rows outside the rank's shard.
- ParallelEngramEmbedding declares a resident table's gather beside a disk
  table's row kernels, and lookup() runs it; the lookup plans, the B12X
  preparation provider and its EngramLookup unit go.

Disk tables (the recipe's) are unchanged.

Tests: the Engram model tests build caps and geometry with the port,
declare the TileLang row kernels instead of preparing B12X plans, and
freeze TileLang's kernel cache where they held B12X's capture guard; a
disk table declares only its reader's kernels; the TileLang disk gather is
checked against its torch reference only (the B12X Triton cross-check
goes); the resident gather is checked against the same reference across
shards, the padded last shard and live counts; the SP prefill tests no
longer skip without B12X.
